(7706350, 1265649, 67258, '<td valign="top">Oh, this is really very good.  My second 10 of the challenge.  I particularly like the way you have included the softly opaque skyline.</td>', 'Oh, this is really very good.  My second 10 of the challenge.  I particularly like the way you have included the softly opaque skyline.', '2021-11-11 12:29:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706351, 1265719, 67258, '<td valign="top">I really like this very much, and would love to see more of your images in this style - looking forward to seeing whose work it is.  In terms of this challenge, I love everything about your submission, with the exception of the ratio - for a novel, it seems a tad wide. 9.</td>', 'I really like this very much, and would love to see more of your images in this style - looking forward to seeing whose work it is.  In terms of this challenge, I love everything about your submission, with the exception of the ratio - for a novel, it seems a tad wide. 9.', '2021-11-11 12:31:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706352, 1265751, 67258, '<td valign="top">Well, I think that this is probably Wendy''s.  What I like:

<br/>the ratio is good for a coffee table book

<br/>the black spine extension works

<br/>the tonal ranged the colour and style of lettering

<br/>Good DOF for the puffin, sharp nearly throughout (just losing it on the most distended part of the belly).

<br/>
<br/>What I am not so keen on:

<br/>The title is a bit naff - or at least, the Peter the Puffin part

<br/>I am pretty sure you have a better photo of a puffin than this - or at least, one with a cleaner belly.  The puffin is sharp, including the critical tip of the bill.  Shame the sandal isn''t facing the camera more.

<br/>
<br/>All in all a good entry, but not amongst my top picks.</td>', 'Well, I think that this is probably Wendy''s.  What I like:

the ratio is good for a coffee table book

the black spine extension works

the tonal ranged the colour and style of lettering

Good DOF for the puffin, sharp nearly throughout (just losing it on the most distended part of the belly).


What I am not so keen on:

The title is a bit naff - or at least, the Peter the Puffin part

I am pretty sure you have a better photo of a puffin than this - or at least, one with a cleaner belly.  The puffin is sharp, including the critical tip of the bill.  Shame the sandal isn''t facing the camera more.


All in all a good entry, but not amongst my top picks.', '2021-11-11 12:38:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706353, 1265755, 67258, '<td valign="top">Fantastic base photo, but the graphic s for a book cover don''t work so well for me.</td>', 'Fantastic base photo, but the graphic s for a book cover don''t work so well for me.', '2021-11-11 12:42:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706354, 1265714, 67258, '<td valign="top">The images, and the way they are combined and processed work exceptionally well as a book cover.  I am not particularly keen on your choice of book title lettering. 7</td>', 'The images, and the way they are combined and processed work exceptionally well as a book cover.  I am not particularly keen on your choice of book title lettering. 7', '2021-11-11 12:44:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706355, 1265327, 67258, '<td valign="top">What I like:

<br/>The high contrast mono palette

<br/>The lighting on your models breasts

<br/>The shape of your models breasts, accenuated by the angle you have chosen

<br/>The title of the book and choice and placement of lettering

<br/>
<br/>What I am not so keen on:

<br/>The ''How to'' lettering - the style seems wrong

<br/>the inclusion in the frame of the fabric (?) either side of your model - makes it look cluttered and distracts from the shape and form.

<br/>The central line that runs vertically from sternum to navel - I''ve never seen this as pronounced before.

<br/>The pose or the angle you have used doesn''t, for me, work for the thighs and crotch area - all I can see is a chicken ready for the oven...</td>', 'What I like:

The high contrast mono palette

The lighting on your models breasts

The shape of your models breasts, accenuated by the angle you have chosen

The title of the book and choice and placement of lettering


What I am not so keen on:

The ''How to'' lettering - the style seems wrong

the inclusion in the frame of the fabric (?) either side of your model - makes it look cluttered and distracts from the shape and form.

The central line that runs vertically from sternum to navel - I''ve never seen this as pronounced before.

The pose or the angle you have used doesn''t, for me, work for the thighs and crotch area - all I can see is a chicken ready for the oven...', '2021-11-11 12:51:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706357, 1265743, 36999, '<td valign="top">What a nice composition for a photo illustration.  The book title font choice is a bit anemic and I would like to see it a is something a little bolder &amp; classic.</td>', 'What a nice composition for a photo illustration.  The book title font choice is a bit anemic and I would like to see it a is something a little bolder & classic.', '2021-11-11 13:58:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706359, 1265702, 36999, '<td valign="top">Well done and very good font choices &amp; treatment.  A very little bit of kerning (adjusting of the spaces between each letter) would make it absolutely perfect.</td>', 'Well done and very good font choices & treatment.  A very little bit of kerning (adjusting of the spaces between each letter) would make it absolutely perfect.', '2021-11-11 14:08:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706361, 1265719, 36999, '<td valign="top">Love your font choices and overall composition of the photo illustration.</td>', 'Love your font choices and overall composition of the photo illustration.', '2021-11-11 14:14:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706363, 1265740, 36999, '<td valign="top">One of my faves in the challenge.  Nicely done.</td>', 'One of my faves in the challenge.  Nicely done.', '2021-11-11 14:16:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706364, 1265751, 36999, '<td valign="top">The photo is remarkable and a nice composition.</td>', 'The photo is remarkable and a nice composition.', '2021-11-11 14:18:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706368, 1265649, 36999, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  Some kerning (attention to the spaces between each letter) would make it perfect.  Examples:  space between "t" and "h" in The is a bit wide as is the space between "g" and "l" in glass and the "p" and "a" in palace.  If you see it now, you will be haunted forever by bad kerning from here on out.</td>', 'Very nice.  Some kerning (attention to the spaces between each letter) would make it perfect.  Examples:  space between "t" and "h" in The is a bit wide as is the space between "g" and "l" in glass and the "p" and "a" in palace.  If you see it now, you will be haunted forever by bad kerning from here on out.', '2021-11-11 14:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706369, 1265744, 36999, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  My highest score given. However, as a graphic designer I see that you didn''t kern the text.  Don''t be alarmed, no one knows about kerning.  It is adjusting the space between each letter (in the word "Us" the space between the u and is a bit wide for example).  Computers can''t do it so you have to do it "by hand".  Its not as easy in PS as in a graphic design but it can be done.  After the challenge ends, I can tell you more if you want.  Learn to kern and it will be perfection!</td>', 'Very nice.  My highest score given. However, as a graphic designer I see that you didn''t kern the text.  Don''t be alarmed, no one knows about kerning.  It is adjusting the space between each letter (in the word "Us" the space between the u and is a bit wide for example).  Computers can''t do it so you have to do it "by hand".  Its not as easy in PS as in a graphic design but it can be done.  After the challenge ends, I can tell you more if you want.  Learn to kern and it will be perfection!', '2021-11-11 14:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706370, 1265664, 36999, '<td valign="top">Very well done overall.  Nice attention to detail with the sticker/seal thing.  I''d like to see the author name not quite as bright as it takes over the composition a bit. Great choice of fonts</td>', 'Very well done overall.  Nice attention to detail with the sticker/seal thing.  I''d like to see the author name not quite as bright as it takes over the composition a bit. Great choice of fonts', '2021-11-11 14:55:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706371, 1265738, 36999, '<td valign="top">Excellent composition and layering of the design elements and attention to details like the "sticker".</td>', 'Excellent composition and layering of the design elements and attention to details like the "sticker".', '2021-11-11 14:55:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706372, 1265565, 36999, '<td valign="top">Love the photo but I don''t love the font choice.  A nice composition overall</td>', 'Love the photo but I don''t love the font choice.  A nice composition overall', '2021-11-11 14:55:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706374, 1265400, 36999, '<td valign="top">"Girls Night Out" could be a little bolder either by font choice or color and I''d move it down just a tad but very nice composition and photo choice.</td>', '"Girls Night Out" could be a little bolder either by font choice or color and I''d move it down just a tad but very nice composition and photo choice.', '2021-11-11 14:55:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706375, 1265632, 36999, '<td valign="top">I don''t like this font.  Never have but it does suit this title &amp; layout.  The space between the "t" and "u" is really awkward.  It could have used a bit (in this case, a lot) of kerning (adjustment of spaces between letters).  The author line could be moved down and made a little smaller so it doesn''t take over the image.</td>', 'I don''t like this font.  Never have but it does suit this title & layout.  The space between the "t" and "u" is really awkward.  It could have used a bit (in this case, a lot) of kerning (adjustment of spaces between letters).  The author line could be moved down and made a little smaller so it doesn''t take over the image.', '2021-11-11 14:56:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706380, 1265740, 30049, '<td valign="top">THIS is what a book cover would look like IMHO.  Not always a "perfect" photo and with a little mystic to it.  Your choice of font is interesting and not one I think that''s in my list of a gazillion.  :-)  Hope you share what it is?</td>', 'THIS is what a book cover would look like IMHO.  Not always a "perfect" photo and with a little mystic to it.  Your choice of font is interesting and not one I think that''s in my list of a gazillion.  :-)  Hope you share what it is?', '2021-11-11 17:08:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7706506, 1265394, 50695, '<td valign="top">my favorite thing about this cover is the way you made the title look like a chart that dips in the middle. The chisels? do look like a bar chart but as far as I know there''s no deeper meaning to it other than that.</td>', 'my favorite thing about this cover is the way you made the title look like a chart that dips in the middle. The chisels? do look like a bar chart but as far as I know there''s no deeper meaning to it other than that.', '2021-11-12 13:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
